                        ],
                        "form": "раска́янии"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "33fb5647-68b0-41af-bc6a-f13f67bdca0f",
                        "entry_id": "2eb4e9fb-8b7e-3ab5-a928-7b12a24260de",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "раска́яниях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bbcc9351-6e18-334c-8eaa-538a15b0f810",
                        "entry_id": "2eb4e9fb-8b7e-3ab5-a928-7b12a24260de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "действие или состояние по значению гл. раскаиваться; сожаление о собственном поступке, признание его ошибочности, порочности"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c854dc5b-e0ff-465d-811b-2a58f05a9c8f",
                                "sense_id": "bbcc9351-6e18-334c-8eaa-538a15b0f810",
                                "text": "Я ощущал раскаяние и сожаление, позднее и напрасное, в сущности, потому что я знал, что ничего нельзя было ни исправить, ни вернуть."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6780d3c5-2557-4114-aa71-401631d4bbe1",
                                "sense_id": "bbcc9351-6e18-334c-8eaa-538a15b0f810",
                                "text": "Он отвечает Черткову: «Два главные чувства вызвало во мне Ваше письмо: отвращение к тем проявлениям грубой корысти и бесчувственности, которые я или не видел, или видел и забыл; и огорчение и раскаяние в том, что я сделал Вам больно своим письмом» (письма этого я не знаю)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e498e4a4-c26d-4324-9937-d826a45a20cf",
                        "source_entry_id": "2eb4e9fb-8b7e-3ab5-a928-7b12a24260de",
                        "source_sense_id": "bbcc9351-6e18-334c-8eaa-538a15b0f810",
                        "target_lang_word": "repentance",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "repentance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81a0d973-6b97-3ee1-a9d3-cf2480e5b3a9",
                                        "entry_id": "16ef1bac-a5a2-3c04-9697-dd98732c4eac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being repentant, penitent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89775ded-8b5e-4c5c-9326-b1b858e12449",
                                                "sense_id": "81a0d973-6b97-3ee1-a9d3-cf2480e5b3a9",
                                                "text": "1678, Bunyan, The Pilgrim's Progress, second period\nGod hath denied me repentance. His words gives me no encouragement to believe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "521ebf6d-3993-3c95-8c26-243eac9b8320",
                                        "entry_id": "16ef1bac-a5a2-3c04-9697-dd98732c4eac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A feeling of regret or remorse for doing wrong or sinning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02c9c09e-93ac-4a54-b6e1-825f7e274d68",
                                                "sense_id": "521ebf6d-3993-3c95-8c26-243eac9b8320",
                                                "text": "And here, shipmates, is true and faithful repentance; not clamorous for pardon, but grateful for punishment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "02a47c2c-651b-4d57-95d5-93824e7a4586",
                        "source_entry_id": "2eb4e9fb-8b7e-3ab5-a928-7b12a24260de",
                        "source_sense_id": "bbcc9351-6e18-334c-8eaa-538a15b0f810",
                        "target_lang_word": "remorse",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "remorse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d88fa4b-782f-3de8-9c22-d489eb9965fd",
                                        "entry_id": "acfdd1de-fc66-3021-a5b9-024ef1652e86",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A feeling of regret or sadness for doing wrong or sinning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0cf6aa0-29ea-4b01-802d-460560933081",
                                                "sense_id": "9d88fa4b-782f-3de8-9c22-d489eb9965fd",
                                                "text": "In criminal proceedings, empirical studies have shown that remorse plays an important role in observers’ judgments of defendants."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52c506e6-5887-42d1-85e0-333685865742",
                                                "sense_id": "9d88fa4b-782f-3de8-9c22-d489eb9965fd",
                                                "text": "Failure, disgrace, poverty, sorrow, despair, suffering, tears even, the broken words that come from lips in pain, remorse that makes one walk on thorns, conscience that condemns . . . —all these were things of which I was afraid."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c6b6773-1201-3138-a788-f3e53fdc1bcd",
                                        "entry_id": "acfdd1de-fc66-3021-a5b9-024ef1652e86",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sorrow; pity; compassion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78692bde-9082-4018-bd4d-301708dac57d",
                                                "sense_id": "9c6b6773-1201-3138-a788-f3e53fdc1bcd",
                                                "text": "This is the bloodiest shame,\nThe wildest savagery, the vilest stroke,\nThat ever wall-eyed wrath or staring rage\nPresented to the tears of soft remorse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "remorse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc37f572-7862-3039-af51-af951338bb36",
                                        "entry_id": "38cd9d37-b1f0-3206-af4d-99f5b0efebc0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To experience remorse; to regret."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01a07b95-5dc8-4449-a293-72a1673798e5",
                                                "sense_id": "dc37f572-7862-3039-af51-af951338bb36",
                                                "text": "And if we look abroad, to take a view of men as they are, we shall find that they remorse in one place, for doing or omitting that which others, in another place, think they merit by."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38c14825-1560-4d23-9622-2cc0df0f27eb",
                                                "sense_id": "dc37f572-7862-3039-af51-af951338bb36",
                                                "text": "When they have accepted their advice and have some upleasant experience then they remorse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64e59efb-f8b0-4f1f-83cd-cf47de4382d7",
                                                "sense_id": "dc37f572-7862-3039-af51-af951338bb36",
                                                "text": "Then with godly sorrow they remorse with a humble heart, and they repent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b3ab5ed0-c4a9-4ec6-929a-0a2193e28a8c",
                        "source_entry_id": "2eb4e9fb-8b7e-3ab5-a928-7b12a24260de",
                        "source_sense_id": "bbcc9351-6e18-334c-8eaa-538a15b0f810",
                        "target_lang_word": "repentir",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "repentir",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "192897e7-45c2-34cf-a9a0-a5999e80fb6e",
                                        "entry_id": "82ef053d-ab46-38a2-80e3-83bee5d3a391",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Action de se repentir."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7ada37b-9298-48ab-b619-6baac15cb5d3",
                                                "sense_id": "192897e7-45c2-34cf-a9a0-a5999e80fb6e",
                                                "text": "Aujourd'hui son bonheur se traduisait par un amour dans la tombe, une épouse dans l'ombre, nul enfant sous le toit et la richesse dans les bras : une vie au gré du destin. Et le cœur de Naalo devint un nid de repentirs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c373ce88-6ff6-440d-84bb-f98227061b72",
                                                "sense_id": "192897e7-45c2-34cf-a9a0-a5999e80fb6e",
                                                "text": "Ravir à l’homme la possibilité d’expier son forfait par son repentir ou par des actes de vertu […] est à mes yeux le plus horrible raffinement de la cruauté."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a108c37-0da4-4ba9-9cb3-9229fc9fb60d",
                                                "sense_id": "192897e7-45c2-34cf-a9a0-a5999e80fb6e",
                                                "text": "Alors, quand toutes les facultés sont suspendues, nous devenons semblables aux démons de l’enfer qui ressentent le remords, mais qui ignorent le repentir."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06d89813-2efd-4d99-9f8c-aa826460a532",
                                                "sense_id": "192897e7-45c2-34cf-a9a0-a5999e80fb6e",
                                                "text": "J’ai ramené au bien et au repentir des misérables qui, un soir, au détour d’un chemin, avaient voulu m’assommer à coups de hache."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "799f7aab-59fa-3354-b4bf-03243e16c128",
                                        "entry_id": "82ef053d-ab46-38a2-80e3-83bee5d3a391",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Trace d’une première idée qu’on a voulu corriger."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Peinture"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70916715-405c-4048-8b21-d68bf9d5dcd7",
                                                "sense_id": "799f7aab-59fa-3354-b4bf-03243e16c128",
                                                "text": "Il y a des repentirs dans ce tableau."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c102043-b523-34fc-a5b0-6aea68b4bdde",
                                        "entry_id": "82ef053d-ab46-38a2-80e3-83bee5d3a391",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cheveux roulés en tire-bouchons, qui pendent des deux côtés du visage. (au pluriel uniquement)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6ed1fdf-8688-494d-bdcc-4f3eb7b1949b",
                                                "sense_id": "5c102043-b523-34fc-a5b0-6aea68b4bdde",
                                                "text": "Malgré son étiquette si pompeuse, l’institution Ouly était une petite école pour rire, tenue par une vieille dame à repentirs, que les enfants appelaient : « bonne amie »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1da15ef-05d3-4f99-8716-3e6f010ac968",
                                                "sense_id": "5c102043-b523-34fc-a5b0-6aea68b4bdde",
                                                "text": "Elle portait, à seize ans, des deux côtés de son blême visage, ces tombantes boucles que l’on nommait des \"repentirs\", et ses yeux bleus rêveurs s’étonnaient près de ses cheveux noirs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "repentir",
